# Recovery-mode init fragment. init.rc imports /init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc
# and ro.hardware is rk30board on this platform.
#
# AOSP's recovery init.rc only drives USB through configfs when sys.usb.configfs
# is 1, and nothing in AOSP ever sets it -- the stock ROM sets it from this same
# file. Without it init takes the legacy /sys/class/android_usb path, which this
# kernel does not implement, so the functionfs mounts fail:
#
#     init: Command 'mount functionfs adb /dev/usb-ffs/adb uid=2000,gid=2000'
#           action=fs took 0ms and failed: mount() failed: No such device
#
# and neither adbd nor fastbootd can come up over USB. Only the serial console
# is reachable.
#
# Two things from the stock file are deliberately left out:
#   - a "console" service: LineageOS' recovery init.rc already defines one, and
#     a second definition is a parse error.
#   - "import /system/etc/init/init.recovery.udc.rc", which starts Rockchip's
#     recovery_udc_detector to publish sys.usb.controller. AOSP init sets that
#     property itself now, in SetUsbController() (system/core/init/init.cpp).

on early-fs
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1

# Windows MS OS descriptors, matching stock. The gadget directories, strings and
# MaxPower are already created by init.rc's own "on fs" block: imports are
# parsed after the importing file, so that block runs before this one.
on fs && property:sys.usb.configfs=1
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/bcdDevice 0x0310
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/bcdUSB 0x0200
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/os_desc/b_vendor_code 0x1
    write /config/usb_gadget/g1/os_desc/qw_sign "MSFT100"
    symlink /config/usb_gadget/g1/configs/b.1 /config/usb_gadget/g1/os_desc/b.1
